id: pm-rl-rsipower
title: Evaluate proposer transfer on a statistically powered tracker corpus
description: "The bounded recursive-improver acceptance uses two distinct meta trackers, below the unchanged ten-sample outer gate minimum; item-level inner bounds are also underpowered on the small chronological cohorts. Plan a larger public tracker/task benchmark with an explicit power analysis, account for correlated fleet work, preserve chronological and meta/audit separation, and repeat equal-budget proposer comparisons without relaxing the promotion gate."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T12:52:29.061Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T05:07:09.921Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T04:31:07.159Z",codex-sol,"Plan: freeze public commit-pinned tracker-disjoint development/meta/audit sources; declare a 0.10 transfer effect, 0.01 promotion margin, alpha 0.05 and target power 0.80 before measuring. Use bounded paired tracker means with task and generation Bonferroni correction. Preserve existing promotion gates and refuse underpowered evidence. Seal replayable corpus/split/evaluation context in SDK-owned items and native history; run one CPU-niced bounded real generation, report all refusals honestly."
  "2026-11-06T04:40:26.177Z",codex-sol,"Corpus frozen before scoring: 31 public MIT source pins, 19 development tasks, 16 meta tasks and 11 audit tasks; corpus digest 7156cf8c85b9941e12e42632c08f27419af69b7b3ee8824545c35def3fee9d49. One unverifiable directory excluded; private/hosted sources never opened. Conservative declared power requires 3062 held-out trackers per task; the available fleet cannot meet this. Proceeding with one bounded diagnostic generation, not claiming powered no-transfer evidence."
  "2026-11-06T04:49:32.441Z",codex-sol,"Runtime adjustment before a complete held-out comparison: stopped the broad diagnostic after 19 development fits and one meta-baseline fit, preserving receipts, reservations and any cancellation transition. A second predeclared diagnostic selects the first three trackers with both tasks in each compartment by SHA-256 repository identity and seed 42, with no score-based selection. One generation, one proposal, 64 updates, 10-minute deadline in an isolated non-git SDK tracker. Native corpus, paired observations and replayable decisions are copied through SDK APIs into this tracker; no evidence side files are published."
  "2026-11-06T04:51:43.385Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable copy: removing only requireProposerTransfer made the underpowered native SDK test fail (exit 1); removing only verifyTransferCorpus made both training/held-out leakage and native split-digest replay tests fail (exit 1). All failures were assertion failures, not import/build failures; each function was restored in finally. Focused corpus/privacy/native replay tests pass 6/6."
  "2026-11-06T05:00:17.159Z",codex-sol,"Real diagnostic completed: 1 generation, 30 fits, 1920 optimizer updates, 5 proposal processes, zero inference tokens, 576.235 seconds including verified native publication. Meta trackers: pm-context, pm-ops, pm-graph. Audit: pm-linear, pm-vcs, pm-starter. Both targets had accuracy 0.50 versus 0.50, paired effect 0.00, simultaneous interval [-1.00,1.00], n=3 and prospective power lower bound 0.00; 3062 trackers per task required. Decision transfer_underpowered, zero promotions, original proposer retained. The audit consequently compares the retained original with itself. No claim of powered no-transfer or improvement. Native result rsipower-bounded-result and digest-addressed corpus/evaluation Decisions retain replayable context. SDK gaps: none encountered; linked tests pass using pm-context none with workspace snapshot (3/3); automatic linked-result storage is disabled by existing project configuration, so this comment retains the result."
  "2026-11-06T05:04:43.881Z",codex-sol,"Targeted native transfer suite passed 8/8, with targeted instrumentation measuring proposer-transfer.ts at 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Full coverage/release suites remain CI-only. Packed candidate replay through the pinned CLI independently reproduced both real meta and audit receipts from native context (2/2), without dataset files or source checkouts. Existing dataset IO regression passed after all-split step revalidation. An earlier mixed regression invocation hit the unchanged 300-second controller timeout under shared load; rerunning that focused group after real-data completion."
